Z||000000||FieroSoul||10-16-2001||07:21 PM||||  This is for anyone who has put a 2.8, or caddy V8 in an 84. How much alteration to the wiring was required in either case. If you did Bubbajoes caddy swap, how well does it work. I am looking for some feedback to decide if I want to do this or just get Ed Parks to drop in a fresh duke. Thanks for all inputs.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-16-2001||07:40 PM||||The 84 Fiero was not designed with a V6 in its product line.  Wiring will be just one of the problems you will encounter putting a v8 into an 84 or a 2.8 into an 84.  Ed would probably talk you into a 3.4 conversion anyway.  How deep is your pocket?  You are talking big bucks for those swaps, unless you have done them before and can do it yourself.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSoul||10-16-2001||09:13 PM||||  In fact Ed is NOT pushing a 3.4 conversion.  He is very honestly recommending the fresh 2.5 instead.  My pockets are deep enough to handle either one.  I am just having trouble making up my mind. All my fault, Ed is a great guy.  I would like honest feedback from some caddy conversion owners.  Bubbajoe makes it sound very easy but I am a little skeptical about the wiring since Ed doesn't recommend it.  ||||reg||6
